_history_tweet_ids": ["2120192425792868414"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/MkOcwA5sHK", "end": 223, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/Brad_Setser/status/2120192425792868414/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120192167821885440", "start": 200, "url": "https://t.co/MkOcwA5sHK"}, {"display_url": "x.com/AntoineBondaz/…", "end": 247, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/AntoineBondaz/status/2120109004143616068", "start": 224, "url": "https://t.co/IsxzPMj4v2"}]}, "id": "2120192425792868414", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 5735, "like_count": 26, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 4, "retweet_count": 7}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120109004143616068", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "I prefer to look at the trailing 12m sum --and on that measure, China's surplus with the EU in the 12ms to October was $360b, up $75b y/y\n\n(and up $200b or a pp or so of EU GDP v pre pandemic levels) https://t.co/MkOcwA5sHK https://t.co/IsxzPMj4v2", "url": "https://x.com/Brad_Setser/status/2120192425792868414"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-11-10T16:27:59.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120191753420509375"], "id": "2120191753420509375", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 31064, "like_count": 186, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 26, "retweet_count": 7}, "text": "Wonder how much better the election would’ve been for republicans if food prices weren’t ripping in the weeks leading up to the vote", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2120191753420509375"}, {"author_id": "3512101", "created_at": "2026-11-10T16:20:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120189753132036155"], "id": "2120189753132036155", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4896, "like_count": 9, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "MOFCOM West accounts are entertaining", "url": "https://x.com/niubi/status/2120189753132036155"}, {"author_id": "733647469305864195", "created_at": "2026-11-10T16:11:56.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120187714532442430"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/3XVc5vNIdc", "end": 228, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/Brad_Setser/status/2120187714532442430/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120187693409636352", "start": 205, "url": "https://t.co/3XVc5vNIdc"}, {"display_url": "x.com/GagnonMacro/st…", "end": 252, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/GagnonMacro/status/2120170965967495252", "start": 229, "url": "https://t.co/hve2ApMkPc"}]}, "id": "2120187714532442430", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 4, "impression_count": 5586, "like_count": 13, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120170965967495252", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "net of gold imports, China's surplus in manufactures is  more less back where it was relative to China's own economy during the initial China shock years (it is obviously way bigger relative to world GDP) https://t.co/3XVc5vNIdc https://t.co/hve2ApMkPc", "url": "https://x.com/Brad_Setser/status/2120187714532442430"}, {"author_id": "3512101", "created_at": "2026-11-10T16:05:25.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120186072365662481"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/sophiacai99/st…", "end": 294, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/sophiacai99/status/2120154675098071431", "start": 271, "url": "https://t.co/723yNWAo0O"}]}, "id": "2120186072365662481", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 26, "impression_count": 6894, "like_count": 86, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 24}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120154675098071431", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "“Staff at the Bureau of Industry and Security, an office within the Commerce Department that oversees U.S. tech exports, had flagged the risk of Nvidia’s advanced chips being diverted to China in “dozens” of reports over recent months. But those warnings have not led to https://t.co/723yNWAo0O", "url": "https://x.com/niubi/status/2120186072365662481"}, {"author_id": "30034124", "created_at": "2026-11-10T15:47:40.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120181606287610217"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 84, "id": "15234407", "start": 79, "username": "CERN"}, {"end": 110, "id": "19732234", "start": 99, "username": "SanfordLab"}, {"end": 219, "id": "3906355332", "start": 207, "username": "DUNEScience"}], "urls": [{"description": "Nearly a mile underground in South Dakota, scientists are building a world-leading experiment to study neutrinos and investigate some of the universe's greatest mysteries, including how the universe took shape after the Big Bang and if neutrinos are the reason our world is predominantly made of matter. Currently, crews from Fermilab, CERN and SURF are assembling large steel beams to form the outer structure of the neutrino experiment’s massive detector modules.", "display_url": "news.fnal.gov/2026/11/constr…", "end": 246, "expanded_url": "https://news.fnal.gov/2026/11/construction-begins-on-massive-underground-neutrino-experiment-designed-to-unlock-the-secrets-of-the-universe/", "images": [{"height": 1601, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120181610754514944/S5tHqeK5?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 2400}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120181610754514944/S5tHqeK5?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 223, "status": 200, "title": "Construction begins on massive underground neutrino experiment designed to unlock the secrets of the universe", "unwound_url": "https://news.fnal.gov/2026/11/construction-begins-on-massive-underground-neutrino-experiment-designed-to-unlock-the-secrets-of-the-universe/", "url": "https://t.co/vrLq8LPW7V"}]}, "id": "2120181606287610217", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 5, "impression_count": 1776, "like_count": 49, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 13}, "text": "Deep underground something exciting is starting to take shape! 🏗️ \n\nCrews with @CERN, Fermilab and @SanfordLab are working together to install massive cryos